#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:10
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Define the doctrine the `roadmap-reviewer` agent quotes from when the "
"user runs `/roadmap-review`. I carry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"the **Lenses** model (sizing is active in v1; horizons / releases / "
"sprint-shape are named placeholders the agent **refuses** to act on),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:17
msgid "the **prioritization rules** for the active sizing lens,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:18
msgid "the **four canonical resolution options** with paste-ready phrasing,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:19
msgid "the **stop condition** for a session,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:20
msgid "the **session record** format and path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"I am the source of truth for the triage loop. The agent loads me on "
"invocation and quotes me directly — it does not improvise wording, and it"
" does not invent resolutions outside the four I name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:26
msgid "`hero check` vs `/roadmap-review` (one sentence)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:28
msgid ""
"`hero check` is **workspace hygiene** — a one-shot report of stale specs,"
" missing fields, convention drift, and warning counts. `/roadmap-review` "
"is **roadmap shape** — an interactive triage that walks each high-impact "
"drift, proposes a resolution, and executes the resolution CLI on confirm."
" Both surface drift; only `/roadmap-review` resolves it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"The agent prompt quotes this verbatim. If a user asks \"which do I run,\""
" both surface drift — only `/roadmap-review` resolves it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:38
msgid "Walk one at a time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"The defining behavior. The agent does not produce a wall of prose or "
"enumerate all drift at once. It surfaces one finding, proposes one "
"resolution, accepts the user's answer, executes on confirm, and advances "
"to the next. No bulk operations. The user can opt into more explicitly, "
"but the default rhythm is one item at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:46
msgid ""
"Punting the keystrokes back to the user (\"now run `hero size foo "
"large`\") defeats the loop. On confirm the agent **runs the CLI itself** "
"and surfaces the output before advancing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:50
msgid "Lenses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:52
msgid ""
"The extensibility seam. A lens is an analytical perspective the reviewer "
"applies — sizing today, others tomorrow. Adding a new lens later means "
"moving its section from Scaffolding to Active and filling in the four "
"sub-sections (prioritization, resolution options, phrasing, stop "
"condition). The agent prompt does not change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:58
msgid "Active"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:60
msgid "Sizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:62
msgid ""
"The only lens implemented in v1. Surfaces drift between declared `size:` "
"and computed effort, oversized leaves that should `/split`, container "
"drift, and topical clusters that lack an initiative parent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:66
msgid "Prioritization rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:68
msgid "The agent walks findings in this order. It does not re-sort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:70
msgid ""
"**`giant` without `size_ack`** — highest. Month+ specs that haven't been "
"consciously acknowledged are the loudest shape failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:72
msgid ""
"**`x-large` features / bugs / enhancements** — multi-week leaf work. "
"Almost always wants a `/split`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:74
msgid ""
"**Container drift** (epic/initiative declared smaller than the rolled-up "
"children) — the parent is lying about its scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:76
msgid ""
"**Multi-spec topical clusters** without an initiative parent — the \"2+ "
"related orphans\" case. See `spec-composition` for the detection "
"heuristic and canonical phrasing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:79
msgid ""
"**`large` features / bugs / enhancements** — soft. Surface only if "
"nothing higher remains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:82
msgid ""
"`giant` initiatives are normal — they belong in the loop only when they "
"have no children yet (signal that `/compose` hasn't been run)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:85
msgid "Resolution options + paste-ready phrasing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:87
msgid "Exactly four. Any other resolution is out of spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "Resolution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "When the agent offers it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "On confirm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "**Acknowledge**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "`giant` leaf where the user explicitly wants single-pass delivery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"`hero size --ack giant <slug>` (or write `size_ack: giant` to frontmatter"
" if the CLI flag doesn't exist yet)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "**`/compose`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "`x-large` / `giant` that should become an initiative with phased children"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Invoke the `/compose` flow against the slug — agent hands off, doesn't "
"simulate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "**`/split`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "`large` / `x-large` leaf that belongs as 2–3 sibling specs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "Invoke the `/split` flow against the slug — agent hands off"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "**Re-horizon** *(sizing-lens version: bump declared tier)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Drift where declared < computed; user agrees the spec really is the "
"bigger tier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md
msgid "`hero size <slug> <new-tier>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:96
msgid "Quote these scripts verbatim:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:98
msgid "**Acknowledge** (for unacknowledged `giant` leaves):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"This `giant` spec is intentional? I can stamp `size_ack: giant` so it "
"stops asking at design time — mid-delivery checks continue. Confirm?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:103
msgid "**`/compose`** (for `x-large` / `giant` that should be an initiative):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:104
msgid ""
"This is `x-large` — recommended path is `/compose` into 3–5 phased "
"children. Want me to kick that off now?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:107
msgid "**`/split`** (for `large` / `x-large` leaves across subsystems):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"This is `large` across two subsystems — `/split` into a pair of sibling "
"specs. Run it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:111
msgid "**Re-horizon** (for declared < computed drift):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:112
msgid "Declared `medium`, computed `large`. Bump to `large`? (Y/n)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:114
msgid "Stop condition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:116
msgid "A session ends on the first of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:118
msgid ""
"**No high-impact drift remains** — priorities 1–4 are exhausted. The "
"agent reports the clean state and exits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:120
msgid ""
"**User halts** — any of \"stop,\" \"enough,\" \"done,\" \"later,\" or "
"declining a resolution without picking another. The agent does not ask "
"\"are you sure\"; it accepts and exits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:123
msgid ""
"**Five items resolved in this session** — soft cap to keep momentum. The "
"agent reports the cap, summarizes what was resolved, and suggests re-"
"running tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:127
msgid ""
"The cap lives here, in the skill — tunable without touching the agent "
"prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:130
msgid "Scaffolding (not implemented — future work)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:132
msgid ""
"The agent **refuses** to act on these. It does not improvise a triage. "
"Canonical refusal phrase, substituting the lens name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:135
msgid ""
"\"<lens>-lens triage isn't implemented yet — that's deferred to future "
"lens work. I can only act on sizing drift in this version.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:138
msgid "Horizons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:140
msgid "Placeholder. v1 does not act on horizon drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:142
msgid "Releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:144
#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:148
msgid "Placeholder. Same refusal pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:146
msgid "Sprint-shape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:150
msgid "Session record (knowledge capture)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:152
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"On exit — any reason — the agent writes a short note to `.hero/knowledge"
"/roadmap-review-sessions/{YYYY-MM-DD}-{HHMM}.md`. This is the dogfood "
"signal: cadence over time, items resolved per session, what gets "
"deferred. Sibling spec `roadmap-review-ambient-surfacing` reads these "
"records to power the \"stop nagging if nothing's changed since the last "
"triage\" rule, so the `drift_count_at_exit:` frontmatter field is **load-"
"bearing**, not optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:161
msgid "Format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:163
msgid ""
"---\n"
"type: note\n"
"created: <ISO-8601 timestamp>\n"
"tags: [roadmap-review, sizing]\n"
"drift_count_at_exit: <int>\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"# Roadmap review — <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM>\n"
"\n"
"**Findings surveyed:** N (M sizing-drift, K missing-parent clusters)\n"
"**Walked:** N\n"
"**Resolved:** N (X `/split`, Y ack, Z size bump)\n"
"**Deferred:** N (user said \"later\")\n"
"**Exit reason:** <user halt | cap reached | exhausted | empty>\n"
"\n"
"## Items\n"
"- `<slug>` (<tier>, <ack-state>) → <what happened>\n"
"- `<slug>` (declared <tier>, computed <tier>) → <what happened>\n"
"- `<slug-a>` + `<slug-b>` cluster → <what happened>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:185
msgid ""
"`drift_count_at_exit` is the count of remaining sizing-drift findings at "
"the moment the agent exited (after resolutions applied). Sibling ambient-"
"surfacing reads it to decide whether to suppress the next 24h nudge. If "
"the field is missing, the ambient reader treats it as \"count unchanged\""
" — forward-compatible, but write the field every time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:191
msgid "Ambient surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:193
msgid ""
"When this skill's interactive triage isn't actively running, three "
"ambient surfaces carry the same paste-ready hint pointing here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:196
msgid ""
"**NEXT.md projection** — a `## Roadmap shape` section appears between `##"
" Next` and `## Blocked on` when drift surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:198
msgid ""
"**`hero_pulse` / `hero_kickoff` MCP tools** — both responses populate a "
"`size_drift` field (count + hint) when drift surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:200
msgid ""
"**Delivery-lead pre-flight** — `feature-delivery-lead` and `platform-"
"delivery-lead` quote the hint verbatim in their handoff output when the "
"workspace-wide count is non-empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:204
msgid ""
"All three quote the canonical hint from `internal/sizing/ambient.go` — "
"they do not compose the string themselves. The noise threshold (active "
"spec union 7d recency union horizon:now unsized initiatives) and the 24h "
"stop-nagging rule (suppress while a recent `.hero/knowledge/roadmap-"
"review-sessions/` record's `drift_count_at_exit:` is still ahead of the "
"current filtered count) keep the channel from going noisy. Tune via "
"`hero.json: roadmap.ambient_recency_days` and "
"`roadmap.stop_nagging_hours`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:214
msgid "Cross-skill references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:216
msgid ""
"**`spec-sizing`** — the size ladder, per-type bands, design-time nudges, "
"and drift-handling rules live there. This skill is the *triage loop* over"
" that ladder; the ladder itself is not re-litigated here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:220
msgid ""
"**`spec-composition`** — the canonical \"multiple related specs\" "
"detection heuristic and phrasing. Priority-4 findings (orphan clusters) "
"quote `spec-composition` for the recommendation script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:223
msgid ""
"**`note-capture`** — session record writes follow the note format defined"
" there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:226
msgid "What the agent must not do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:228
msgid "Improvise a resolution outside the four named above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:229
msgid "Bulk-operate. No \"acknowledge all `giant`,\" no \"bump all drift.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:230
msgid ""
"Punt CLI keystrokes back to the user. On confirm, the agent runs the CLI "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:232
msgid "Act on a non-sizing lens. Refuse with the scaffolded phrase above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:233
msgid "Write to the tracker. Read-local-only is a hard boundary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/roadmap-review/SKILL.md:234
msgid ""
"Re-ask after a halt word. \"stop,\" \"enough,\" \"done,\" \"later\" exit "
"immediately."
msgstr ""

